### Refunds 

Sunbit requires that you submit a refund within 180 days from the original payment using the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) or [Refunds API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/create.md). This is the maximum the payment method allows. Your return policy determines what you offer customers.

Refunds for Sunbit payments are asynchronous and take up to 5 minutes to complete. You can’t cancel Sunbit refunds.

#### Refund process 

Sunbit refunds are never processed as reversals. When you issue a refund, Sunbit cancels any remaining scheduled payments and returns any amounts the customer has already paid. The customer sees the update reflected in their Sunbit account.

#### Tracking refunds 

To check a refund’s status, open the payment in the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) and click **View details** on the refund entry. You can also [retrieve the Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/retrieve.md) and check its `status` field.

Stripe notifies you of the final status through a `refund.updated` or `refund.failed` *webhook* (A webhook is a real-time push notification sent to your application as a JSON payload through HTTPS requests) event. [Verify webhook signatures](https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks.md#verify-events) to confirm that events came from Stripe. You can also use Stripe’s [public IP addresses](https://docs.stripe.com/ips.md) for network allowlisting. When a refund succeeds, the [Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/object.md) status changes to `succeeded`. If the refund fails, the status changes to `failed` and Stripe returns the amount to your Stripe balance. You must refund the customer using another method.

### Disputes 

There’s no set time limit for customers to file Sunbit disputes.

#### Dispute process 

1. **Dispute opened**: Sunbit opens a dispute. Stripe immediately withholds the disputed amount from your balance. You have 12 calendar days to submit evidence.
2. **Decision**: Sunbit reviews your evidence and issues a final decision within 35 calendar days of dispute creation.

#### Dispute notifications 

When Sunbit disputes are opened, Stripe notifies you through:

- Email
- The [Stripe Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/disputes)
- A [charge.dispute.created](https://docs.stripe.com/api/events/types.md#event_types-charge.dispute.created) event

The dispute reason is available in the Dashboard and in the `reason` field of the [Dispute object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/disputes/object.md). The evidence submission deadline is available in the Dashboard and in the `evidence_details.due_by` field of the Dispute object.

#### Responding to disputes 

You have 12 calendar days from dispute creation to submit evidence.

We request that you upload compelling evidence proving that you fulfilled the purchase order [using the Stripe Dashboard](https://docs.stripe.com/disputes/responding.md#respond). This evidence can include the:

- Tracking ID
- Shipping date
- Record of purchase for intangible goods, such as IP address or email receipt
- Record of purchase for services or physical goods, such as phone number or proof of receipt
- Record of refund (for purchases you’ve already refunded)

You can submit evidence and manage Sunbit disputes in the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/disputes) or programmatically using the [Disputes API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/disputes/update.md). In the Dashboard, go to the **Needs response** tab, click the disputed payment, then click **Counter dispute** to submit your evidence, or **Accept dispute** to accept the loss. To submit evidence through the API, upload supporting files using the [Files API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/files/create.md) and include the returned file IDs when you update the [Dispute Evidence object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/disputes/update.md).

#### Dispute outcomes 

If Sunbit resolves the dispute in your favor, Stripe returns the disputed amount to your Stripe balance.

If they rule in favor of the customer, the balance charge becomes permanent.

#### Fees and appeals 

Sunbit doesn’t charge dispute fees. If Sunbit resolves the dispute in your favor, Stripe returns the full disputed amount to your Stripe balance with no fees deducted.

Sunbit dispute decisions are final. You can’t appeal a dispute after Sunbit issues its decision.

#### Fraud and liability 

Customers must authenticate Sunbit payments by logging into their Sunbit account. This requirement helps reduce the risk of fraud or unrecognized payments. While Sunbit covers losses incurred from customer fraud, Stripe might contact you on behalf of Sunbit and request to stop or pause shipment before any losses are incurred. Comply promptly with these requests.

